[{:db/id "q-36008/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "f14f122f-ac73-57fd-9b99-000f27d1e194" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36008/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "36ef5ed4-1f1d-583b-8ec4-0ca44da0b84a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36008/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "76a62ba4-8d2b-5c2c-813f-55a188da8c2d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36008/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "8a5d7ff8-6be9-52f9-a738-a92b9c9a3ff2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36008/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "c0ce0c15-affc-5f3a-8003-35e6001668fe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36008/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "896dcd52-2934-5d16-967a-67e5193ad3ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-36008/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-36008/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-36008/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-36008/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-36008/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-36008/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-36008" :question/id #uuid "2527bbd8-ce59-54a7-8446-7823452ff16c" :question/math-academy-id "q-36008" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938271/assets/279c3cd6084423d913186f4ba467ea50d0f794cf54773785777cb8841f5c2ca1.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\n- $x\\in (-3,-1]$\n- $x\\in [-1,3]$\n- $x\\in [0,1]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-3,-1]$ and on $x\\in [0,1].$  Indeed, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938271/assets/0388335095ed530ce07d278f82be5eb3bff14859db64b6e9ec47da27861bb657.png)\n\n    \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval. $x\\in [-1,3]$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938271/assets/522b5661aaf9b7640c305b8cefd06f49cc8eed590f3ae736fc6720e6165bc3a9.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-36008/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-36008"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-36011/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "a09ec9a7-8948-5881-9d7a-0d5559742687" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36011/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "9e196ccb-8c57-5e2a-9599-3601ac27e60e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36011/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "7b82cedc-8826-5d7a-8049-bd7e75b056f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36011/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "c45c5c26-1b43-53c2-a227-4d0e3eee9613" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36011/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "db9e6792-fef2-58a4-ba35-7719d3d97ef6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36011/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf31fb09-af3e-5bd4-8dbf-0959c7520f3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-36011/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-36011/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-36011/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-36011/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-36011/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-36011/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-36011" :question/id #uuid "d650f0a9-fd5d-507e-a056-8206ec6f99b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-36011" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938271/assets/b02c2e94e144935f0ff96846cd51b5a969fa8f884a7ca1d09abb231b7c945232.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible? \n\n- $x\\in (-4,-2)$\n- $x\\in [-2,3]$\n- $x\\in [-3,3]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.  \n\n- The given function is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-4,-2)$ and $x\\in [-2,3].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938271/assets/53fe88780b2ccb7522d2f1baa711162ec99300c2a2d4da29bba9ca532026cd07.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on  the interval $x\\in [-3,3]$  because some lines will  intersect the curve at more than one point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938271/assets/63cee4fc05ab17a8e69d9bfae578fa83c24d73e4677065a54a33a25e0871e718.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-36011/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-36011"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-66483/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "94f97e89-f832-5e56-b367-8a64a99a0eaa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66483/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "c571ab9d-03e1-549f-af91-68e832ac65f5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66483/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "2fc46fb9-f5fa-5a1b-9e20-b7d031a52ab6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66483/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "6e39ae33-384f-5db3-95e7-98d3ff078d79" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66483/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "1695ddc5-efe0-57d6-83d2-1e4411875614" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66483/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fc1dde06-b0cb-5b44-8493-384e4ca0292c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-66483/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-66483/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-66483/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-66483/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-66483/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-66483/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-66483" :question/id #uuid "1d69f632-8fdd-59a0-ac8c-5d011c3cdeaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-66483" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=1-x,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$\n- $x\\in (0,\\infty )$\n- $x\\in (-2,2)$" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is a linear function with slope $-1$ and $y$-intercept $1,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938271/assets/73d9277c040ae457ba6d96e162574edbeeef965d181fa6011ca4ab0e4644bd82.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- Since the function is invertible on $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ it is also invertible on $x\\in (0,\\infty )$ and $x\\in (-2,2).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-66483/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-66483"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-66679/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "28217140-f0c6-596b-b769-9908ebb6394c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66679/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "f77d6579-fe5c-56b9-875b-c633c7094d54" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66679/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "84cfbddf-296c-5eb0-bb5e-8521ded059cc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66679/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "9fd6e907-c50b-526e-9ab7-04df18a64abb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66679/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "cf83e1a4-53a2-5468-81a2-96d167b220ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66679/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a528a080-2ee9-5522-a3ae-06023d1ae817" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-66679/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-66679/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-66679/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-66679/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-66679/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-66679/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-66679" :question/id #uuid "888d7ea8-2f15-562e-8a8d-c02982ae9999" :question/math-academy-id "q-66679" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=(x-1)^{2}-2,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$\n- $x\\in (1,\\infty )$\n- $x\\in (-1,3]$" :question/worked-solution "The graph of the function $f(x)=(x-1)^{2}-2$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y={x}^{2}.$\n\n- Translate it by $1$ units to the right,  to get $y=(x-1)^{2}.$\n\n- Finally, translate $y=(x-1)^{2}$  by $2$ units down to get $f(x)=(x-1)^{2}-2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938271/assets/f53a4f97166877085c90acc01e3f8d0c6ac7bb3f704bbfb792d747122d314013.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$ and $x\\in (1,\\infty ).$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938271/assets/b088c8ed1974a7c259dd54f85aec7a124579981971babfe8dee0313ca23b6458.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-1,3].$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938271/assets/b3af13782a01213bb09fdeef38fbeb3fbca3f41348036e6786b4efa74a0166b4.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-66679/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-66679"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-108795/selection/8893f166b98b9446101ce8475968b2f3ba283ac6676341b35819ccdd3dd32f98" :answer/id #uuid "13fa0eb4-2662-5191-a558-3d224d6037d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in [-2,4]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108795/selection/4fa3f6e6befad2868dfa97273aba2b8c62674e30bc92f1a50e5274de9cf7ab5e" :answer/id #uuid "d4cc1890-c18d-5a13-a9ce-350ca623f0e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in [-2,0]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108795/selection/62773e2f885c16d8ec4a4aed668ce0ced8aefb0da96d586642dbcb1356ee3562" :answer/id #uuid "53f0ea70-840c-52a5-8f8e-7e1f6ff3a93b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in [0,4]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108795/selection/7d3426e57add872f854ec53df212125117e03c02ab00fad19821d66e66e4b654" :answer/id #uuid "d117117c-35e4-5cb4-8557-ed472252206b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (0,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108795/selection/ba42c31bb975d91b3e305151da0f1554f326b3456274cdd98cf657fe923632ab" :answer/id #uuid "d826f68a-e6a8-5ed6-8a2e-5e486563dfcb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-2,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108795/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ad221038-ac8d-5361-bc3e-62a8aae5cac6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-108795/selection/62773e2f885c16d8ec4a4aed668ce0ced8aefb0da96d586642dbcb1356ee3562" :answer-field/choices ["q-108795/selection/8893f166b98b9446101ce8475968b2f3ba283ac6676341b35819ccdd3dd32f98" "q-108795/selection/4fa3f6e6befad2868dfa97273aba2b8c62674e30bc92f1a50e5274de9cf7ab5e" "q-108795/selection/62773e2f885c16d8ec4a4aed668ce0ced8aefb0da96d586642dbcb1356ee3562" "q-108795/selection/7d3426e57add872f854ec53df212125117e03c02ab00fad19821d66e66e4b654" "q-108795/selection/ba42c31bb975d91b3e305151da0f1554f326b3456274cdd98cf657fe923632ab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-108795" :question/id #uuid "f9b1d4b5-ce4c-5ef1-a359-cd6d35ef33f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-108795" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938271/assets/def2afaad6d1f74ca3ac8833ed6e35efea1296b324ef5a14c2d9513983a63456.png)\n\nDetermine the largest interval on which the function $f(x)$ (shown above) is invertible." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the domain of our function is $x\\in [-2,4].$\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ does not pass the horizontal line test on the interval $x\\in [-2,0].$ In this case, the horizontal line $y=-2$ intersects the graph at more than one point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938271/assets/033b9e827caf4fc89d4b179c769f5115254c811953f93caf33d0959bfd063235.png)\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on the interval $x\\in [0,4].$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938271/assets/4c91aa95131758065b1d8befe7c69895dc51d2f984a04cc8f06932a32e552792.png)\n\nTherefore, the largest interval on which the function is invertible is:\n\n$$\nx\\in [0,4]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-108795/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108795"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
